{"availability":"available","full":"typephp-php/typephp","name":"typephp","description":"Pure PHP Transparent Runtime Enforcement of PHPdoctype, with support for generics, type-arrays, ","category":"Other","language":"PHP","stars":58,"forks":6,"created":"2026-08-03T03:25:55Z","updated":"2026-10-18T06:50:38Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://typephp-php.github.io/docs/","topics":[],"demo":"https://typephp-php.github.io/docs/playground.html","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T09:16:45.721Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T09:16:45.721Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T09:16:45.721Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:01:06.546Z","stars":56,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-13T04:15:02.846Z","stars":58,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-15T13:02:16.343Z","stars":58,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-18T09:16:45.721Z","stars":58,"forks":6}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["No transpilation. No build steps. No C-extensions.","Drop TypePHP into your existing codebase and let your DocBlocks scream when types fail.","TypePHP is a transparent, pure-PHP runtime type checker. You don't have to refactor a single line of your codebase, set up complex build toolchains, or compile C-extensions. Simply run your existing code, and TypePHP will enforce your extended PHPDoc contracts (generics, array shapes, key-of/value-of extractions, and scalar refinements) dynamically at runtime."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/typephp-php/typephp/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"296a6437f29faecdac85ec04d6a217abc1d506f00e2db2c34da610e070fc2557","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:06.711Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T09:16:45.888Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"No transpilation. No build steps. No C-extensions.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/typephp-php/typephp/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"296a6437f29faecdac85ec04d6a217abc1d506f00e2db2c34da610e070fc2557","sourceUrl